# R1 — gate the inverse transform + reconstruction on C's own predicate

date: 2026-08-13
host: mac (Apple aarch64, 12 logical cores), box shared with another agent —
      every timed run wrapped in `~/bin/measlock`. NEITHER SIDE NICED.
base: 8179a7d94 (R2 landed)   cand: this commit
build: both arms `RUSTFLAGS=-C llvm-args=-align-all-functions=4`, no
       `target-cpu=native`. Control arm = a byte-IDENTICAL SECOND COPY of the
       base binary (equal md5), run in the same session on the same grid.
harness: rust/tools/perf_ab.sh — interleaved paired rounds, randomised order,
       one untimed warmup inside each sample.
noise floor: [0.9843, 1.0190]. Anything inside it is NULL whatever its sign.

## The three per-site dead-proofs

The port inverse-transformed and reconstructed unconditionally. C gates on
`ctx->mds_do_spatial_sse || (!is_inter && cand_bf->cand->block_mi.tx_depth)`
(`product_coding_loop.c:4783-4784`), chroma twin `full_loop.c:2313`, single-TX
luma `:5727`. All-intra pins `spatial_sse_full_loop_level = 3`
(`enc_mode_config.c:10010`), so `mds_do_spatial_sse` is false at MDS1 (`:7025`)
and MDS2 (`:7047`) — C inverts NOTHING there.

Each site's proof is an exhaustive scan of every occurrence of the binding in
its own scope, not "the immediate caller does not use it":

1. **MDS1 luma** (`for &ci in order.iter().take(n1)`, a 161-line loop). `out` is
   a `let` local to one iteration; it is never stored, moved or returned. Every
   non-comment occurrence of `out` in the whole loop body is a single line:
   `None => (out.eob, out.bits as u64, out.dist, lambda)`. No `.recon`, no
   `.qcoeff`, no `.cul`. Nothing outside the loop can observe it.
2. **CfL alpha search** (`plane_cost` closure, 34 lines). `out` is closure-local
   and the closure's tail expression is `(out.dist, out.bits)` — the only other
   occurrence. C's `av1_cost_calc_cfl` reaches `svt_aom_full_loop_uv` with
   `is_full_loop = 0`, so the `is_full_loop && mds_do_spatial_sse` gate is false
   for every alpha tried.
3. **non-CfL chroma re-cost** (`u_nc` / `v_nc`). Inside the 876-line
   `cfl_gate && cfl_uv_follows` block the only occurrence beyond the two
   bindings is `u_nc.dist + v_nc.dist`. A whole-file scan finds ZERO other
   mentions of either name. C recomputes this cost through `svt_aom_full_loop_uv`
   with `is_full_loop = 0` (`product_coding_loop.c:3800-3860`), which likewise
   never inverts. Its RATE deliberately comes from `u_out`/`v_out`, not from
   these.

Three of three proved; none deferred.

Two structural safeguards, because a proof is only true of today's code:
* the flag is an explicit `need_recon` parameter, NOT `spatial_dist` reused —
  `spatial_dist == false && need_recon == true` is legal the moment a depth-1
  neighbour prediction needs the reconstruction;
* the effective predicate is `need_recon || spatial_dist`, so a future caller
  that mislabels `need_recon` still gets correct spatial distortion;
* the skipped buffer is `Vec::new()`, not a zeroed block: a consumer that
  appears later gets an index panic, never a plausible black block.

